{
  "uid": "glamdb-podman",
  "title": "GlamDB · Podman containers",
  "description": "Official prometheus-podman-exporter 1.21.2 reads the existing VM-local Podman Unix socket and exports actual container names. This is Podman on Linux inside the VM, not Kubernetes or macOS container accounting. Memory usage is max(memory.current - memory.stat inactive_file, 0), source/live qualified for this Podman runtime. The reported memory ceiling falls back to VM RAM for unbounded containers. PIDs are cgroup tasks including threads, not a process count. CPU system seconds from this Podman build have an upstream unit defect and are omitted; use the exact cgroup dashboard. Separate cgroup dashboard provides charged/anonymous/file/unevictable memory, IOPS, PSI, throttling and faults. Stopped containers retain inventory/state but have no live resource stats.",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "timezone": "browser",
  "tags": [
    "glamdb",
    "local",
    "standard-collectors"
  ],
  "refresh": "15s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "container",
        "label": "Container",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(podman_container_info{job=\"podman\"},name)",
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(podman_container_info{job=\"podman\"},name)",
          "refId": "container"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "refresh": 1,
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Source and scope",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Official prometheus-podman-exporter 1.21.2 reads the existing VM-local Podman Unix socket and exports actual container names. This is Podman on Linux inside the VM, not Kubernetes or macOS container accounting. Memory usage is max(memory.current - memory.stat inactive_file, 0), source/live qualified for this Podman runtime. The reported memory ceiling falls back to VM RAM for unbounded containers. PIDs are cgroup tasks including threads, not a process count. CPU system seconds from this Podman build have an upstream unit defect and are omitted; use the exact cgroup dashboard. Separate cgroup dashboard provides charged/anonymous/file/unevictable memory, IOPS, PSI, throttling and faults. Stopped containers retain inventory/state but have no live resource stats."
      }
    },
    {
